    "result": "Done. What changed in `src/app/sections/about/about.tsx` (plus the icon pipeline):\n\n**The critical (team photo) is blocked, not skipped.** Both routes to the asset failed this pass:\n- Figma MCP `download_assets` → Starter-plan tool-call paywall.\n- REST fallback `GET /v1/images?ids=182:2560` → `{\"status\":429,\"err\":\"Rate limit exceeded\"}`.\n\nThis is run-wide, not section-specific: hero, the-fleet, how-it-works and footer all still carry the same `photo-placeholder` TODO, and the project has no raster asset at all. I left the token placeholder and the TODO (which already records `1114×740`, cover, `-170px -31px`) rather than writing a binary - binaries are auto-reverted after the turn, so shipping an `<img src>` would just have produced a broken image on top of a missing one. The frame itself (radius, `#ECECEC` hairline, `aspect-ratio: 774/520`, chip inset) is already measured pixel-exact.\n\n**What I did fix:**\n\n1. **Lint error** - the inline 4px `<svg>` now lives in the icon pipeline: added `src/assets/icons/icon-bullet-arrow.svg` and regenerated `src/components/icons/index.tsx` with `npm run icons:generate`. The generator is a pure function of the icons directory, so regenerating only appends the new export and is safe next to the other agents.\n\n2. **8 of 11 position deltas closed.** The trades labels were hug-width; in Figma each `Bullet` is `sizing fill` inside a gap-24 `Line`, so the label spans `(659-24)/2 - 16 = 301.5px`. Every reported delta confirms it exactly (Tesla `36+265=301`, Microsoft `65+236=301`, … and the full-width last row `134+509=643=659-16`), so the span is now `flex-1`. Same mechanism inverted for the eyebrow: Figma's \"Clippership\" hugs at 83px, `432-349=83`, so it is now `w-fit`. Neither is a visual change - both are the measured box.\n\n3. **Deliberately left alone:** the three `Ex-…` credential deltas all report an identical 174px, which implies a constant 210px Figma width, not a hug (the strings render 218/193/151px natural). Card geometry already matches spec §4c and the reviewer measured it as correct, so I did not touch it on an ambiguous signal.\n\nTypecheck and lint are clean (the one remaining warning is in devlooper's own `dl-source-loc-loader.cjs`). `npm run build` refused to start - another agent holds the Next build lock - so the loop's own build will be the first full run of this change.",
